        "original_id": "f5be39d4-6865-5566-879e-4e1d377c62c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Ironweed\n- People: Lauro Escorel, Hector Babenco\n- Places: Albany, New York, Jay Street at Lark Street, Albany Rural Cemetery, Miss Albany Diner, North Broadway\n- Buildings: Miss Albany Diner\n\nFacts:\n- The Miss Albany Diner, formerly known as Lil's Diner, was built in 1941 in Albany, New York.\n- The Miss Albany Diner is located at 893 Broadway, one of the oldest streets in Albany.\n- In 1987, the film Ironweed made Lauro Escorel more known internationally.\n- Ironweed was another film by Hector Babenco.\n- Major portions of Ironweed were shot on location in Albany, New York.\n- Ironweed used Jay Street at Lark Street, Albany Rural Cemetery, and the Miss Albany Diner on North Broadway as filming locations.",
